---
// Terms and Conditions page. DRAFT (2026-09-05), pending a professional legal /
// data-protection review before go-live (launch runbook GATE 0). Mirrors the
// privacy.astro layout. Specifics set by Ben 2026-09-05: satisfaction re-clean
// within 24h of the END of the appointment, one re-attendance, via the assistant
// (paper trail); complaints acknowledged within 3 working days, resolved within
// 10 working days of acknowledgement; invoices due within 14 days, interest on
// overdue in line with the Bank of England base rate. Owner still to confirm:
// public-liability insurance wording (deliberately omitted until confirmed, L-009/
// D-015), the cancellation notice period, and deposit-refund terms. See D-031.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions | Intelligent Carpet Cleaning"
  description="The terms on which Intelligent Carpet Cleaning provides carpet and upholstery cleaning across Cheltenham and Gloucestershire, including our satisfaction promise and complaints procedure."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
    <p>The terms on which we provide our carpet and upholstery cleaning services.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="legal-wrap">
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: 5 September 2026. Please read these terms. They apply to the quotes we give, the bookings you make, and the work we carry out. They do not affect your statutory rights.</p>

    <h2>Who these terms are with</h2>
    <p>These terms are between you and Mark McClymont, a sole trader trading as Intelligent Carpet Cleaning, based in the Cheltenham and Gloucester area of Gloucestershire ("we", "us", "our"). You can reach us on <a href="tel:01452452356">01452 452356</a> or at <a href="mailto:hello@intelligentclean.co.uk">hello@intelligentclean.co.uk</a>. Our postal address is available on request.</p>

    <h2>Quotes and prices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A quote given by our assistant, or otherwise before we attend, is an estimate based on the information and any photographs you provide. In the large majority of cases the quoted price is the price you pay.</li>
      <li>If, on arrival, the size or condition differs materially from what was described, we will explain and agree any change with you before carrying out additional work. No extra charge is applied without your agreement.</li>
      <li>Our prices are the final price payable. We are not VAT registered, so no VAT is added.</li>
      <li>A flat out-of-area surcharge applies outside Cheltenham, Gloucester and Winchcombe, and is shown before you book.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Booking and deposit</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A 10% deposit secures your booking and is applied to your final bill.</li>
      <li>If we have to cancel or cannot attend, your deposit is refunded in full.</li>
      <li>Standard daytime bookings are confirmed automatically. A booking that would finish later in the day is held and confirmed by Mark personally before it is final.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Payment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>For domestic work, the balance is due on completion of the clean.</li>
      <li>Where we invoice you, including commercial and contract work, payment is due within 14 days of the invoice date.</li>
      <li>We may charge interest on overdue invoices in line with the Bank of England base rate, calculated daily from the due date until payment is received.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cancellations and rescheduling</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Please give us at least 48 hours' notice if you need to cancel or rearrange, so we can offer the slot to someone else.</li>
      <li>If we cannot gain access at the agreed time, or an appointment is missed without notice, we may retain the deposit to cover the time set aside.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Access, parking and preparation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Please make sure we can access the property at the agreed time, and that there is somewhere reasonable to park nearby. Where paid parking at the site is unavoidable, the cost may be added to your bill.</li>
      <li>Please remove small items and breakables from the areas to be cleaned. We can move larger furniture where it is safe to do so; a furniture-moving surcharge may apply.</li>
      <li>Please tell us in advance of anything we should know, such as loose seams, prior damage, delicate fibres, or pets.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our service and results</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We identify the fibre and construction and match the cleaning method to your carpet, taking reasonable skill and care.</li>
      <li>Cleaning improves the appearance and hygiene of a carpet, but cannot always remove every mark. Some older stains, dye damage, bleach marks and general wear are permanent, and we will tell you honestly where that is the case.</li>
      <li>Drying times and results depend on the fibre, the condition of the carpet, and the conditions on the day.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our satisfaction promise</h2>
    <p>If you are not happy with your clean, let us know within 24 hours of the end of your appointment <a href="/book">through our assistant</a>, and we will return once to put it right at no extra charge. This is in addition to your legal rights and does not affect them.</p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We carry out our work with reasonable skill and care.</li>
      <li>We are not responsible for pre-existing damage, wear, or defects, or for damage arising from a condition of the carpet or item that could not reasonably have been identified before cleaning.</li>
      <li>Nothing in these terms limits or excludes our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited or excluded.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If something has gone wrong, we want to put it right. Raise it <a href="/book">through our assistant</a>, or contact us on <a href="tel:01452452356">01452 452356</a> or <a href="mailto:hello@intelligentclean.co.uk">hello@intelligentclean.co.uk</a> with your booking details and what happened. We will acknowledge your complaint within 3 working days and aim to resolve it within 10 working days of that acknowledgement, keeping you updated if it needs longer.</p>

    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>We handle your personal information in line with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your statutory rights</h2>
    <p>Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights as a consumer under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 and other applicable law.</p>

    <h2>General</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We may update these terms from time to time. The version on this page when you book is the version that applies to that booking.</li>
      <li>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales and are subject to the jurisdiction of its courts.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero{margin-top:70px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--navy-dark) 0%,var(--navy) 100%);padding:3rem 2rem;text-align:center;}
  .page-hero h1{font-family:"Raleway",sans-serif;font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.5rem;}
  .page-hero p{color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:1rem;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;}
  .legal-wrap{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;color:var(--text-mid);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.95rem;}
  .legal-meta{color:var(--text-light);font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:2rem;}
  .legal-wrap h2{font-family:"Raleway",sans-serif;font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.8rem 0 0.6rem;}
  .legal-wrap p{margin-bottom:0.8rem;}
  .legal-wrap ul{margin:0.5rem 0 1rem;padding-left:1.3rem;}
  .legal-wrap li{margin-bottom:0.3rem;}
  .legal-wrap a{color:var(--teal);text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;}
  .legal-wrap a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}
</style>
